  "budget_note": "Full redesign; gameplay unimplemented and old-code reuse unassessed. Owner-selected mercenary/city campaign, recipe memory/cooldowns and system upgrades. Delivered 606-recipe Markdown draft for four proposed mercenaries: original 600 plus six shared Rare/Legendary next-round manual-grab enhancements, with shared/exclusive rarity pools; numeric values and new character/timing rules are proposals, not playtested balance. No graphics or game functionality in this pass. Prototype-readiness review delivered: settle magnet supply, turn rules, enemy threats and fight/reward boundaries before a playable build. One-character three-fight sample is proposed, not approved. Full permanent-upgrade and modifier catalogues are later work. Preserve the STYLE anchor, 16B planning/rear gathering/intents, 16C attack perspective, unique city surroundings and support for at least 20 parts each in shot and shield. Timeline unconstrained; zero time fields mean unset. Owner selects baseline ingredient options with Collect/Precision on a claw screen, one ordinary haul per turn and one manual timing grab per fight. Loadout includes full-screen recipe crafting and an in-fight shop. Load then select targets then Fire leads to surviving enemies; End Turn / Defend supports no-shot rounds. Death shows Game Over with a gloating AI. Precision recipes enhance the saved next-round grab without granting another use. Raise conflicts for owner resolution: Shield/non-Ammo activation, gathering-part fitting, Load/undo and shop timing. Supply amounts, bonus bands and exact effect/reward/reset details remain open; no implementation.",
